quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  9,7,"How can the (treacherous) idolaters have any (valid) treaty with Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him)? But as for those with whom you made a treaty near the Sacred Mosque (at al-Hudaybiya), so long as they remain steadfast with you (in fulfilment of their promise), remain steadfast with them. Indeed, Allah loves the God-conscious."
  9,8,"How (can they have a treaty)? If they prevail over you, they will not observe, in your case, any ties of relationship (or principle of diplomacy) or treaty. They please you with their mouths (by flattering words) while their hearts contain the opposite. And most of them are disobedient."
  9,9,"They have sold the revelations of Allah for a paltry price and have turned from His way. Indeed, evil is what they have been doing."
  9,10,"In the case of a believer, they observe neither any bond of relationship nor any (term of) treaty. It is they who are the transgressors."
  9,11,"But if they repent, establish the prayer and give the alms due, then they are your brethren in faith.* We make the messages clear for people who understand."
  9,12,"If they break their pledges after having made their treaty and openly revile your religion (causing a potential threat to state security), then fight the leaders of militancy (to pre-empt their aggression and invasion). Indeed, they have no (commitment to their) pledges. (This pre-emptive action is needed) so that they might stop (their offensive designs)."
  9,13,"Will you not fight the (treacherous) people who broke their pledges (violating the peace treaty), conspired to expel the Messenger ([blessings and peace be upon him] from Mecca) and initiated (hostilities) against you first? Do you fear them? But Allah is most deserving that you should fear Him if you are (true) believers."
